            <ArticleTitle>Prevention of Alzheimer disease: The roles of nutrition and primary care.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>30-5; quiz 35-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/01.NPR.0000463782.57968.c2</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Risk factors for developing Alzheimer disease include hypercholesterolemia, hypertension, obesity, and diabetes. Due to lack of effective treatments for Alzheimer disease, nutrition and primary prevention becomes important.</AbstractText>
